== Implementation ==
backend/app/vcf_validation.py: canonical_contig/normalize_contigs (primary chromosomes only; a chr-named file is
  returned as the same string object); contig_length_evidence (GRCh38 / GRCh37 / neither); lengths join the
  declared-build set, so a GRCh37 length is refused as GRCh37 (message names the contig and both lengths) and a
  GRCh38/GRCh37 mix is CONFLICTING; a length that is neither is refused; BCF magic refused as NOT_VCF naming BCF;
  REF check after the row count: any mismatch refuses the file (REFERENCE_ALLELE_MISMATCH, or
  UNSUPPORTED_REFERENCE_BUILD when >=10 compared and >=half differ); a silent header with >=1 verified position is
  read as GRCh38 and the warning states the count; rename warning last.
backend/app/reference_check.py (new): the comparison; first base, upper-cased; a position counts once.
backend/app/coverage.py: gVCF reference blocks (<NON_REF> or <*>, END beyond POS) counted as
  gvcf_block_positions; variants_only is false for such a file; gvcf_warning.
backend/app/main.py: /analyze and /coverage give the gVCF warning; /analyze withholds the all-genes-gated
  (research-format/SNP-array) diagnosis when it applies.
scripts/scientific_hash_policy.json: reference_check.py and reference_alleles.json enrolled (94 core paths).
docs/input_requirements.md: how the build is recognised; REF, gVCF, BCF, chromosome-name and multi-sample sections,
  each with its command. User-facing messages name no tool (test_no_developer_strings): my first BCF and gVCF
  messages named bcftools and GATK, failed that guard, and now point to the input requirements page instead.

== Existing tests changed, each because the planned behaviour changed ==
- test_build_and_binary_detection: a headerless file whose one row is a required position with GRCh38's REF is now
  read as GRCh38 with the evidence warning (design item 3); a new test keeps the "assuming GRCh38" path for a file
  with nothing to compare.
- test_vcf_validation TestAccepts.test_missing_build_warns_but_accepts: same change.
- test_coverage_endpoint, test_coverage_gate, test_evidence_validity: their generated files wrote REF A at every
  required position, which no GRCh38 file does; they now write GRCh38's base (tests/grch38.py, from the same data
  file). No expectation changed.
- test_evidence_crosscheck: B3's adversarial files no longer reach PharmCAT. Its fixture now switches off the REF
  check and the contig rename, so its tests still prove B3's second line on its own; a new test checks the front
  door (wrong-REF files 400, the 10-named file answered as the base). Clients are built per call because
  test_deployment.py reloads app.main, which strands a client built at import (its 400s lost error_code).

